QUESTIONS=['(answered: apply_fixes.py normalises every expanded conclusion to the printed pointing, Joseph 27 Nov) Qui tecum pointing (your ruling; Rubr. gen. XI.2, M39 p. 52): in my group the Mi…', '(answered: new field "inter", added for Quad6w, Pasc6s, Pent0w, Pent0s) Second collects inside a Mass (Quad6w p. 154 "Deus, qui pro nobis Fílium tuum cr…', '(answered, RULINGS 27 Nov 22:15: read from G28 pp. 261-262; still open as a chant task) Pent0s, Ember Saturday of Pentecost (M39 pp. 254-256; Rubr. gen. XIII.3, p. 53 "post quamlibet Lectionem … dicuntur Alleluia eo modo, quo ibidem signantur"): the Missal prints an Alleluia verse after each of the five lessons; masses.js has only Laudate (after the Epistle) and gr 6986 "Benedictus es" from G p. 15 (Advent hymn) in the place of the Alleluia "Benedíctus es Dómine Deus patrum nostrórum: et laudábilis in sǽcula. Allelúia". Read these from G28 (pp. 261-262)?', 'EmbSatSeptS "Sabbato IV Temporum (forma brevior)": the Missale O.P. 1939 has no shorter form of the September Ember Saturday (pp. 291-296 print only the full Mass with five lessons; the Rubricae generales pp. 47-55 give none). masses.js marks its chants "dm" (1959) and lists only three readings. Drop it from the 1939 menu, as C1s ("only use the Missal")? Its texts are fixed like EmbSatSept meanwhile.']
NOTES=['WARNING for the coordinator: the live data (applied before 22:xx) has three A2 values with junk from the 1933 OCR, because an intermediate fix entry carried them: Quad6 Passion "spíritum., et genuflectitur¿." and "cum. eo"; Quad6t Passion "exspirávit.,."; Pasc0h Lesson "descendepost¿ Pascha runt¿". The current A2.json entries for these three paths (old = the live value) correct them; please apply.', 'Recheck (27 Nov, after A4\'s finding): prop.py dropped inserted punctuation when the Missal side had only a C/S speaker mark plus punctuation, and could not show capital changes after a word read as "I". Fixed (insertions now shown; CAP? note). All FIXED Masses rechecked with recheck.py: 30 more commas/semicolons found and confirmed on the scan (Quad6 and Quad6t Passions, Quad6 or, Quad5s Lesson, Pasc0 or and Gospel, Pasc1 Gospel, Pasc4 Epistle), plus Pasc2 se, Pent0m or, Pent0w or (I had wrongly marked these OK). Stray-line scan of the whole group: found "cum. eo" and "spíritum.,." in the Quad6 Passion, the running head "In die Ascensionis Dómini" in the Asc Lesson, "Peni tecostes" and dropped "Cum" in the Pent0 Lesson; all fixed. No other stray lines found in A2 texts.', 'Holy Week (Quad6-Quad6h): in the 1939 form the Mass page is drawn from data/holyweek_text.js (HW_TEXT), not from orations.js/readings33.js (js/app.js massSequence, "if (HT)"). HW_TEXT is a scan-faithful transcription; I used it only as a cross-check (tools/audit/scripts/A2/hwcmp.py) and confirmed every difference on the scan. Found in HW_TEXT: Quad6w Lesson I has "Salvátor" where the Missal p. 154 prints "salvátor".', 'Text layer: reliable for words, capitals and mid-line punctuation; it drops punctuation at line ends near the gutter (prop.py keeps the site\'s there, "eol?"), reads initial "í" as "I", and garbles some words (VAR?, site word kept). Line-end punctuation is checked by eye on the scan.', 'The 1939 Missal spells cena/cenáculum/cenávit; the site has cœna.', 'The orations from Divinum Officium (src "Tempora/…") have Roman punctuation (commas around "quǽsumus, Dómine"; "," / "." where the Missal has ";" and ":"), and Roman spellings.', 'The readings (from the 1933 OCR, tools/m33) have OCR slips and lines dropped at column or page breaks.', 'Expanded conclusions are kept as the site has them; only their type (Per Dóminum / Per eúmdem / Qui tecum / Qui vivis) is compared with the Missal (Rubr. gen. XI.2, M39 p. 52).', 'Passion headings: the site titles all three Passions "Sequéntia sancti Evangélii…"; the Missal prints "Pássio Dómini nostri Jesu Christi secúndum …".', 'bible/en/Lucas.txt 13:7 has the slip "Cut it done" (Douay "Cut it down"); fixed in EmbSatSept/EmbSatSeptS English only.', 'Pent23 Epistle (p. 303): the Missal prints an asterisk before "Itaque fratres mei caríssimi" (Phil 4:1); not reproduced on the site; its use is not explained in the Rubricae generales (pp. 47-55).', 'fin4.py fix (28 Nov): a "subs" entry whose new text contains the old (e.g. adding an incipit) was applied twice when the earlier entry was already live; now a sub is skipped when its result is already present. One such doubled entry (EmbFriSept English Lesson) was caught before saving and removed.']

OPEN=['Pent0s: the Alleluias after Lessons I-V still to be read from G28 pp. 261-262 (RULINGS 22:15).', 'Pasc6s: the Litany (p. 243) and the private-Mass Introit Cum sanctificatus (p. 244) are not on the site.', 'Pent17 English Gospel lacks "Accessérunt ad Jesum Pharisǽi" (for the incipit script). Pent0s.inter Lesson III English (DM) says "O Lord" where the Latin has "omnípotens Deus" (DM verbatim).', '"inter" items carry extra keys: "chant" (true = said after the chant that follows the lesson), "en_src" ("dm"/"ai"), and optional "rubric".', 'SAME proposals can hide "quǽsumus, Dómine," (DO punctuation; the Missal prints "quǽsumus Dómine,"): every oration from Pent2 on was read on the scan.', 'EmbSatSept/EmbSatSeptS.inter collect after Lesson III (Præsta … sic nos ab épulis): the 1959 English says "almighty God" where the 1939 Latin has "Dómine" (DM verbatim). The Missal prints after the fifth collect "Secunda Oratio A cunctis, p. 287, vel sequens Concéde (B.M.V.), juxta Rubricas" with Secret Tua Dómine and Postcommunion Sumptis (pp. 294-296): for the coordinator\'s 2nd/3rd prayers (addiv.js). Rubric p. 291 for the coordinator: the Ember commemoration in a feast\'s Mass takes the collect Præsta (p. 292), not Omnípotens.', 'Pent20 English Gospel begins with Jn 4:46a ("He came again therefore into Cana … wine."), which the Latin (p. 299 "Erat quidam régulus") lacks: for the Gospel-opening script.', 'AscVig: the Missal prints the Rogation memoria and the third prayer de Cruce inside this Mass (pp. 234-235); check that the app adds them (2nd/3rd prayers, addiv.js); English Gospel opens with Jn 17:1a "These things Jesus spoke," (Latin "Sublevátis Jesus óculis"): for the incipit script.', 'Dedicatio Paschal Alleluias (p. 2*): second Alleluia Christus resúrgens (existing 6484, G p. 208) and in Ascensiontide Ascéndens Christus (existing 5526, G p. 240); masses.js has only Adorabo (5217). Check G28/G50 pp. 354-355 before wiring (D.md).']
